| Question                                          | Short Answer                                                            |
| ------------------------------------------------- | ----------------------------------------------------------------------- |
| What is JDBC?                                     | API to connect and interact with databases from Java.                   |
| Which package contains JDBC classes?              | `java.sql`.                                                             |
| Steps in JDBC?                                    | Load driver → Connect → Statement → Execute → Process → Close.          |
| Difference between Statement & PreparedStatement? | PreparedStatement supports parameters (`?`) and prevents SQL injection. |
| What is ResultSet?                                | A table of data returned by a SELECT query.                             |
| What are executeQuery() and executeUpdate()?      | `executeQuery()` → SELECT; `executeUpdate()` → INSERT/UPDATE/DELETE.    |
| What is SQLException?                             | Exception thrown for DB-related issues.                                 |
| What does Class.forName() do?                     | Loads JDBC driver class into memory.                                    |
| Can we skip Class.forName()?                      | From JDBC 4.0 (Java 6+), drivers auto-load if JAR is in classpath.      |
| How do you close DB resources safely?             | Use try-with-resources or finally block.                                |


| Component         | Purpose                       | Example                         |
| ----------------- | ----------------------------- | ------------------------------- |
| DriverManager     | Manage DB connections         | `DriverManager.getConnection()` |
| Connection        | Represents DB link            | `Connection con = ...`          |
| Statement         | Execute queries               | `stmt.executeQuery()`           |
| PreparedStatement | Execute parameterized queries | `ps.setString(1, "Murali")`     |
| ResultSet         | Holds query result            | `rs.next()`                     |
| SQLException      | Catches DB errors             | `catch(SQLException e)`         |
